8. Standard Adoption and Integration Strategy

For AIPS to become a community standard, it must solve a concrete pain point for a well‑defined early adopter group. We target MLOps engineers and ML reproducibility researchers, who currently lack a machine‑readable, verifiable contract between business stakeholders and modelling pipelines.

Concrete adoption step:
must develop an open‑source MLflow plugin that accepts an AIPS specification as a model artifact. The plugin will:

· Validate the AIPS syntax and invariants.
· Version the specification alongside model code and data.
· Display the specification’s denotation (objective, constraints, action space) in the MLflow UI.
· Provide a comparison view for A/B testing of multiple formulation variants.

This plugin directly integrates AIPS into a widely adopted ML lifecycle platform (MLflow has > 10 million monthly downloads). Success will be measured by plugin adoption metrics (stars, issues, downstream integrations) and by whether peer research groups begin including AIPS artifacts in their published projects.

In addition, must propose AIPS as a new category in the NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks track, encouraging the community to contribute validated specifications for common business problems.

