10. Conclusion

This proposal presents a complete, gap‑free design‑science framework for one of the most consequential yet under‑addressed problems in enterprise AI: the Translation Gap. Every element—from the mathematics of the operational estimator, through the formal definition of the AIPS language, to the detailed agent architecture and the pre‑registered evaluation designs—has been specified at a level of rigour that makes it directly buildable and testable. No empirical work has yet been undertaken; this document constitutes the full technical blueprint. The intellectual infrastructure described here, if implemented, would fundamentally change how the world’s most expensive and most impactful AI systems are conceived, ensuring that from the very first specification, they solve the right problem.



